<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Seu d'Urgell</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Seu d'Urgell is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segre">Segre</a> in the Catalan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, just south of Andorra. It has been the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Urgell since late Roman or Visigothic times, and its 12th-century cathedral of Santa Maria is one of the finest Romanesque buildings in Catalonia. Since the agreements of 1278 its bishop has been co-prince of Andorra.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-seu-durgell.jpg" alt="La Seu d'Urgell" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brain Pics · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catedral_seu_d%27urgell.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
